WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.580
In this short video,

2
00:00:01.580 --> 00:00:04.821
you'll see how to build a mobile app prototype with Lovable,

3
00:00:04.821 --> 00:00:08.116
publish it, and test it on your phone, with no coding at all.

4
00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.838
Lovable is an AI app builder.

5
00:00:10.838 --> 00:00:13.204
You describe what you want in plain English,

6
00:00:13.204 --> 00:00:16.754
and it builds a working website or app that you can click through,

7
00:00:16.754 --> 00:00:18.367
change, and share with a link.

8
00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:22.519
For user experience design, that's really powerful.

9
00:00:22.519 --> 00:00:25.981
You can turn an idea into a realistic prototype in minutes,

10
00:00:25.981 --> 00:00:28.329
test it with real users on a real phone,

11
00:00:28.329 --> 00:00:31.087
and update it from their feedback the same day.

12
00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:35.149
And if you don't code, you can still build websites,

13
00:00:35.149 --> 00:00:37.451
apps and simple systems for your projects,

14
00:00:37.451 --> 00:00:40.684
so you can focus on your users, the content and the design.

15
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:45.441
There are three parts: build the app, publish it, and put it on your phone.

16
00:00:46.633 --> 00:00:49.603
Start by creating a free account at lovable.dev.

17
00:00:49.603 --> 00:00:53.887
The free plan gives you five build credits a day, and needs no credit card.

18
00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.555
Next, write a clear prompt.

19
00:00:56.555 --> 00:00:59.280
Describe each screen, the navigation and the look,

20
00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.351
and say it's for a phone-sized screen.

21
00:01:01.351 --> 00:01:05.447
The guide includes the full prompt we used for a wardrobe app called Closet.

22
00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:09.619
After a minute or two, your app appears in the preview.

23
00:01:09.619 --> 00:01:12.605
Improve it with small requests, one change per message.

24
00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:15.103
If something breaks, History lets you go back.

25
00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:17.911
Keep an eye on your credits.

26
00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.673
Small, focused requests cost less than big ones.

27
00:01:21.867 --> 00:01:24.125
When you're happy, click the Publish button.

28
00:01:24.125 --> 00:01:26.016
Publishing from the button is free,

29
00:01:26.016 --> 00:01:29.205
and you'll see your website address, ending in lovable.app.

30
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.091
Set who can view it to Public, so your testers can open it with the link.

31
00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:37.628
Click Publish, and your website is live.

32
00:01:37.628 --> 00:01:41.935
Remember, the live site is a snapshot, so publish again after any changes.

33
00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:46.822
To get it onto your phone, use Chrome's QR code for the published page,

34
00:01:46.822 --> 00:01:48.744
and scan it with your phone's camera.

35
00:01:49.933 --> 00:01:52.019
On Android, open the Chrome menu,

36
00:01:52.019 --> 00:01:56.128
tap Install and create shortcut, then choose Install page as app.

37
00:01:56.128 --> 00:02:00.195
On an iPhone, use Safari's Share button, then Add to Home Screen.

38
00:02:01.400 --> 00:02:06.008
Tap the new icon, and your prototype opens full screen, just like a real app.

39
00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:09.490
Now you're ready to test it with users.

40
00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:13.248
Follow the step-by-step guide below this video for every detail.

41
00:02:13.248 --> 00:02:13.835
Good luck!

